UNIT isarray
KIND FUNCTIONAL
ORACLE-CLASS deterministic

# Pure value-mode type-checker. No seam (no clock/RNG/env/fs/net). One argument,
# read-only, no mutation of the argument or any ambient state. Returns a real boolean.

SIG isarray(value: any) -> boolean

DEPENDS-ON none

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PROVENANCE OF THE EXPORT SHAPE  (verified against the real source + runtime)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Source (index.js, verbatim, 5 lines):
#
#     var toString = {}.toString;
#     module.exports = Array.isArray || function (arr) {
#       return toString.call(arr) == '[object Array]';
#     };
#
# The exported value is chosen ONCE, at module load, by the expression
#   `Array.isArray || <polyfill>`:
#   * If the host realm has Array.isArray (every Node >= 0.x, every modern browser),
#     the export IS Array.isArray itself -- the native function reference, BY IDENTITY
#     (verified: `require('isarray') === Array.isArray` -> true; .name === 'isArray';
#     .length === 1).
#   * Only in a (now-historical) realm LACKING Array.isArray does the export become the
#     toString-brand polyfill.
#
# THE TWO IMPLEMENTATIONS AGREE on every input this unit's generator can emit, and on
# every realistic value. They DIVERGE on exactly one constructed class of object:
# a non-array whose brand is forged to "[object Array]" via Symbol.toStringTag, e.g.
#   const o = {}; o[Symbol.toStringTag] = 'Array';
#   native Array.isArray(o) === false   (CORRECT for v2.0.5)
#   polyfill toString.call(o) === '[object Array]' -> true   (divergent)
# THE AUTHORITATIVE BEHAVIOR FOR isarray@2.0.5 IS THE NATIVE Array.isArray BEHAVIOR
# (the `||` short-circuits to the native ref in every host that has it). The blind
# re-emitter MUST therefore reproduce `Array.isArray` semantics (the genuine-array
# partition below), NOT the toString brand. Such Symbol.toStringTag objects are OUT OF
# ENVELOPE for the generator anyway (Symbols do not survive the factory codec), so the
# graded set never contains a case where the two implementations differ -- but the
# specification is pinned to native semantics so there is no ambiguity.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BEHAVIOR  (the true/false partition -- exact)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# isarray(value) returns a REAL boolean primitive (typeof result === 'boolean'),
# NEVER a truthy/falsy non-boolean, NEVER undefined.
#
# RETURNS true  IFF `value` is a genuine Array exotic object -- i.e. an object created
#   by the Array constructor / an array literal / Array.of / Array.from / a spread, or a
#   subclass instance of Array (class X extends Array). Concretely, true for every value
#   for which the native Array.isArray returns true:
#     []                       -> true   (empty array literal)
#     [1, 2]                   -> true
#     [[1], [2]]               -> true   (nested arrays: the OUTER value is an array)
#     new Array(3)             -> true   (sparse / holes; still an array)
#     new Array(1, 2, 3)       -> true
#     Array.of(7)              -> true
#     (subclass) new (class extends Array)() -> true
#     a FROZEN array Object.freeze([1])      -> true
#
# RETURNS false for EVERYTHING ELSE, including (exhaustive over in-scope classes):
#     {}                                   -> false   (plain object)
#     { a: 1 }                             -> false
#     { 0:'a', 1:'b', length: 2 }          -> false   (ARRAY-LIKE / arguments-like: NOT an array)
#     a real `arguments` object            -> false   (array-like, but not an Array)
#     ''                                   -> false   (empty string)
#     'abc'                                -> false   (string -- even though indexable)
#     42, 0, -1, 3.14                      -> false   (numbers)
#     true, false                          -> false   (booleans)
#     null                                 -> false
#     undefined                            -> false
#     NaN                                  -> false
#     Infinity, -Infinity                  -> false
#     10n / any bigint                     -> false
#     new Set([1,2])                       -> false
#     new Map()                            -> false
#     /re/  (RegExp)                       -> false
#     new Date()                           -> false
#     new Uint8Array(3) / any TypedArray   -> false   (TypedArrays are NOT Arrays)
#     Buffer.from([1]) (Node Buffer)       -> false   (a Uint8Array subclass; NOT an Array)
#     new Number(5), new String('x'),      -> false   (boxed primitives)
#       new Boolean(true)
#     Object.create(Array.prototype)       -> false   (inherits Array.prototype but is
#                                                       not an Array exotic object)
#
# DOCUMENTED EDGES:
#   * EMPTY array []            -> true  (length 0 does not matter; it is an array)
#   * SPARSE array new Array(3) -> true  (holes do not matter)
#   * NESTED: only the top-level argument is classified; [[...]] is itself an array -> true
#   * The function does not throw for ANY input (Array.isArray never throws; the polyfill's
#     toString.call also never throws for any value, including null/undefined). NO throw path.
#   * The argument is never mutated and never coerced; classification is by internal
#     [[Class]] / exotic-object kind, not by reading .length or any property.
#
# CALL/ARITY NOTES:
#   * The function's declared arity is 1 (.length === 1). Calling with zero args
#     (value === undefined) -> false. Extra args beyond the first are ignored.

ORACLE value -> oracle.json

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SCOPE
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IN-CONTRACT LOGIC (reproduce exactly): the genuine-array partition above == native
#   Array.isArray semantics; return a real boolean; no throw; no mutation; arity 1.
# CARRIED DATA: none. Pure function, no literal tables.
# OUT-OF-CONTRACT: none (no stateful mutator, no side API).
# OUT OF ENVELOPE (documented, NOT emitted by the generator -- non-round-trippable
#   under the factory codec, and would only probe the native/polyfill divergence which
#   is pinned to native above):
#     * live function values (typeof 'function')              -> would be false
#     * Symbol values                                         -> would be false
#     * objects carrying a forged Symbol.toStringTag === 'Array' -> native: false
#       (v2.0.5's authoritative answer), polyfill: true. PIN: native -> false.
#   A blind engineer reconstructs all three from this spec without seeing them in inputs.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EMISSION SHAPE  (DEFAULT-EXPORT unit -- exportName is null)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The blind re-emitter MUST emit an ES module whose DEFAULT export is the function value:
#     export default function isarray(value) { return Array.isArray(value); }
# NOT a named export, NOT module.exports, NOT `export const ... `. The harness imports the
# default binding and calls it as a function of one argument. Reproducing native
# Array.isArray semantics (e.g. by delegating to Array.isArray, which IS what the package
# resolves to) is the faithful implementation.

PROVENANCE isarray@2.0.5, git://github.com/juliangruber/isarray, MIT license, file index.js
